<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lastovo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lastovo is an island in the southern Adriatic, part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>, lying about 80 kilometres west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dubrovnik">Dubrovnik</a>. It came under the Republic of Ragusa in the thirteenth century and kept its own statute and a degree of self-government until the republic's fall. After 1815 it passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and from 1920 to 1947 belonged to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, and much of the island is now a nature park.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lastovo.jpg" alt="Lastovo" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dijana Župan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Skrivena_luka,_Lastovo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
